00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:39.020
In the last video, I suggested math wasn’t
the language of the universe and you had a

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:39.900
lot to say.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:45.000
frib75 and a few others took the extreme opposite
position and said math wasn’t even a language,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.900
which is an interesting perspective.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.820
They agree the symbols we use to represent
math are a language,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.300
but math itself is something more fundamental
to the universe.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.670
Whether you’re writing math symbols
or writing out the translated English sentences,

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.850
you’re doing math.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.940
You’re just going through logical steps
and those steps are the real math.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:06.740
But I see two problems with this argument:
One!

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.220
Some logic leads to paradoxes and the real
universe doesn’t have those.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:10.900
Two!

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.440
Things like photons and electrons don’t
calculate the paths they travel.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.680
They just move.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.780
We’re the ones that do the calculating.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:22.780
ScienceMaths2012 asked what might actually
be a more testable question:

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.920
Can the universe be axiomatized?

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.080
In math, there are a bunch of things you can
prove and a short list of things you can’t.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.960
The things on that short list are called “axioms,”
which are things we must assume to be true

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.880
for math to even work in the first place.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:40.270
Like "a" times zero equals zero regardless of what “a” is.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:44.400
If you can find and agree on a set of axioms
for our physical laws

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.220
then you could say the universe is inherently
mathematical.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.940
The problem here is that physics can’t even agree whether or not

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.960
Newton’s laws or conservation of energy and momentum is more fundamental

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.360
let alone whether or not either of them are an axiom.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.400
Thedarkfly said the symbols I used in
the video are specifically for English.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.200
Is that true?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.920
I've always been under the impression that the scientific community agreed on the symbols that we use

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.040
including the parts of the community in countries with languages that aren’t latin-based.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.400
Let me know in the comments.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.180
Rick Clark pointed out that units of measure
are completely made up by humans.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.020
That’s true.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.300
They’re completely arbitrary.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.960
But a lot of theoretical work is done completely without regard for units at all

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.600
The equations can be written to show relationships between measurements that are true for any units.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.590
So I’m not sure this piece of information
works in my favor.

